                <pb facs="0689" n="681" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg681"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.981/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-23T12:00:00+01:00">September 23,
                        1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1390. For the Department’s additional information: The suggestion of Consul
                    General Davis that he and Haering return eventually to Warsaw as stated in my
                    telegram of last night was based on a wish to make such arrangements as might be
                    decided upon regarding the Government premises and property there as well as to
                    take steps to safeguard the effects of the officers who have left.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
